{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791591160,"nonce":"Xt3VXsgjjFDNrLLg9umC1ftKKAg=","message":"Rust side checked: draw_shadow emits a shadow primitive with no test on blur, spread or offset, and the callers (paint/basic.rs, layered.rs, layout_renderer.rs, motion.rs) loop over props.shadow without a guard. So an outer shadow with blur 0 and spread 0 does reach the shader, and the shader's own guard is what drops it. The Rust-side bounds padding (paint.rs, composite-layer AABB) already adds max(spread, 0); only the vertex shaders lack it.","files":null}]}